{"tool_name":"crosstalkdb","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"crosstalkdb","home":"http://crosstalkdb.bmb.sdu.dk","summary":"Repository and statistical tools for directly determined PTM crosstalk based on long peptides measured by mass spectrometry. Focus on histone proteins.","addition_date":"2015-04-24T14:33:56Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-25T14:16:22.081807Z","tool_type":["Database portal","Web API","Web application"],"collections":["Proteomics","ms-utils"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:crosstalkdb","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"jenseno@bmb.sdu.dk","name":"Ole N\u00f8rregaard Jensen","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"email":"veits@bmb.sdu.dk","name":"Veit Schw\u00e4mmle","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]},{"email":"jenseno@bmb.sdu.dk","name":"Ole N\u00f8rregaard Jensen","typeRole":["Support"]},{"email":"veits@bmb.sdu.dk","name":"Veit Schw\u00e4mmle","typeRole":["Support"]},{"name":"bmb.sdu.dk","typeEntity":"Institute","typeRole":["Provider"],"url":"http://computproteomics.bmb.sdu.dk"}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://crosstalkdb.bmb.sdu.dk/faces/welcome.xhtml;jsessionid=4f15bf82d38197f552e8000e7121"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["proteomics.bio.tools"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Expression data","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2603"},"format":[{"term":"CSV","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3752"}]}],"operation":[{"term":"Expression analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2495"},{"term":"Expression data visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0571"},{"term":"Multiple sample visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3744"},{"term":"Statistical calculation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2238"},{"term":"Visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0337"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Expression data","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2603"},"format":[{"term":"CSV","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3752"},{"term":"PDF","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3508"},{"term":"XML","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2332"},{"term":"xlsx","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3620"}]},{"data":{"term":"Protein interaction data","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0906"},"format":[{"term":"CSV","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3752"},{"term":"PDF","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3508"},{"term":"XML","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_2332"},{"term":"xlsx","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3620"}]},{"data":{"term":"Protein interaction data","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0906"},"format":[{"term":"CSV","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3752"},{"term":"SVG","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3604"}]},{"data":{"term":"Sequence image","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2969"},"format":[{"term":"CSV","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3752"},{"term":"SVG","uri":"http://edamontology.org/format_3604"}]}]}],"name":"CrosstalkDB","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"veits@bmb.sdu.dk","publication":[{"doi":"10.1074/mcp.o113.036335","metadata":{"abstract":"Mass spectrometry (MS) is a powerful analytical method for the identification and quantification of co-existing post-translational modifications in histone proteins. One of the most important challenges in current chromatin biology is to characterize the relationships between co-existing histone marks, the order and hierarchy of their deposition, and their distinct biological functions. We developed the database CrossTalkDB to organize observed and reported co-existing histone marks as revealed by MS experiments of histone proteins and their derived peptides. Statistical assessment revealed sample-specific patterns for the co-frequency of histone post-translational modifications. We implemented a new method to identify positive and negative interplay between pairs of methylation and acetylation marks in proteins. Many of the detected features were conserved between different cell types or exist across species, thereby revealing general rules for cross-talk between histone marks. The observed features are in accordance with previously reported examples of cross-talk. We observed novel types of interplay among acetylated residues, revealing positive cross-talk between nearby acetylated sites but negative cross-talk for distant ones, and for discrete methylation states at Lys-9, Lys-27, and Lys-36 of histone H3, suggesting a more differentiated functional role of methylation beyond the general expectation of enhanced activity at higher methylation states. \u00a9 2014 by The American Society for Biochemistry and Molecular Biology, Inc.","authors":[{"name":"Aspalter C.-M."},{"name":"Jensen O.N."},{"name":"Schwammle V."},{"name":"Sidoli S."}],"citationCount":62,"date":"2014-01-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Molecular and Cellular Proteomics","title":"Large scale analysis of co-existing post-translational modifications in histone tails reveals global fine structure of cross-talk"},"pmcid":"PMC4083120","pmid":"24741113"}],"topic":[{"term":"Protein interactions","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0128"},{"term":"Protein modifications","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0601"},{"term":"Proteomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0121"},{"term":"Proteomics experiment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3520"}],"validated":1},"bioschemas":{"name":"CrosstalkDB","home":"https://bio.tools/crosstalkdb","summary":"Repository and statistical tools for directly determined PTM crosstalk based on long peptides measured by mass spectrometry. Focus on histone proteins.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:crosstalkdb/db/crosstalkdb.bmb.sdu.dk","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"sourcecode":{"interpreted":false}},"project":{"build":{